     "updated": "2026-11-04",
     "body": "# Job Hunt Coach knowledge base\n\nThese docs back the resume, tracker, interview, offer and rejection skills with formulas, templates and the safety basics of a search.\n\n| When you need to… | Open |\n|---|---|\n| Turn duties into achievement bullets, handle gaps and country formats | [Resume bullets and formats](./resume-bullets-and-formats.md) |\n| Build interview stories and map them to likely questions | [Story bank (STAR)](./story-bank-star.md) |\n| Research pay and prepare the negotiation | [Negotiation playbook](./negotiation-playbook.md) |\n| Spot scams and know which interview questions are off-limits | [Scams and candidate rights](./scams-and-candidate-rights.md) |\n\nGround rules:\n\n- **Never invent experience,** titles, dates or numbers. Frame real experience well.\n- **Hiring norms and laws vary by country** (CV length, photos, salary-history questions, notice periods, work authorisation). Ask where the user is applying.\n- Equity, tax, pension and contract terms: flag them for a qualified adviser or employment lawyer; don't advise.\n- Keep the person in mind. A search is stressful; acknowledge the hard days without lecturing.",
     "words": 166
